Theorem RL-20: thread-shared values use atomic RC

  Preconditions:
    - RL-20 governs thread-shared atomic RC per Annex E §AIMS
      Non-Atomic RC: "Thread-shared values SHALL use atomic RC."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - A value is thread-shared (per the RL-18a derivation) when it escapes
      (Locality >= HeapEscaping) AND a call-graph path carries it across a
      thread boundary (spawn / channel / FFI export).
    - Shipped: target-system rule; realize/decide.rs consumes Locality.
    - depends-on RL-18a (thread-shared derivation).

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v that is thread-shared (escapes across a thread boundary):

      (P1) Atomicity decision: RL-20 emits atomic RC (CAS) for v.

      (P2) Soundness: a thread-shared value's reference count may be mutated
           concurrently by multiple threads; only atomic read-modify-write
           (CAS) prevents a data race that would corrupt the count (and cause
           a use-after-free or a leak). Non-atomic RC on a thread-shared value
           is UNSOUND.

    RL-20 is the safety floor of the non-atomic-RC optimization: whenever the
    analysis cannot prove thread-locality, atomic RC is mandatory.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — thread-shared atomicity:
      The verifier confirms a HeapEscaping value crossing a thread boundary is
      classified thread-shared (derives_thread_shared = true) and receives
      atomic RC. Negative-direction witness: a thread-shared value MUST NOT
      use non-atomic RC (a data race on the count would corrupt it) —
      asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl20_thread_shared_atomic;
        thread-shared atomicity check + negative witness; emits Fail on a
        misclassification or a non-atomic selection for a thread-shared value)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-20 via thread-shared atomicity (a value escaping across a thread boundary -> atomic CAS RC) with a negative-direction witness rejecting non-atomic RC on a thread-shared value (data race), grounded in the RL-18a thread-shared derivation
